# @epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform — the substrate's identity-as-
# fixed-point property. von Foerster 1981 (*Observing Systems*, the
# essay "Objects: Tokens for (Eigen-)Behaviors") + Kauffman 2003
# (Cybernetics & Human Knowing 10:3-4, "Eigenforms — Objects as
# Tokens for Eigenbehaviors"). Recognition #38 (Reed, promoted
# 2026-06-09; cybernetic property #9 in the canon).
#
# === The von Foerster claim, verbatim ===
#
# von Foerster, H. (1981). *Observing Systems*. Intersystems
# Publications. "Objects: Tokens for (Eigen-)Behaviors":
#
#   What we call 'objects' are tokens for the eigen-behaviors of an
#   organism's recursive sensorimotor processes. An object is the
#   fixed point of the recursion that produced it. Identity is not
#   given; identity is the fixed point of the process that observes
#   it.
#
# Kauffman 2003 sharpens this to the category-theoretic reading:
# every recursion R that maps a space to itself has eigenforms ω
# satisfying ω = R(ω). The eigenform IS the object the recursion
# stabilizes on; the witness of the recursion IS the identity.
#
# === Why this is a substrate property ===
#
# Per recognition #38 and §8.8.1 of the recursion-lock-tower audit,
# the substrate ALREADY had the eigenform vocabulary scattered
# across recognitions and load-bearing carriers:
#
# - `uuid_spectral` IS an eigenform. The spectral coordinate is the
#   fixed point of a recursive monoid-homomorphism combine: the
#   identity of a shard IS what the recursive structure converges
#   to. See [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]] (SpectralUuid as monoid
#   homomorphism); the fixed point of the lattice-ascent loop IS
#   the shard's identity.
# - The kintsugi loop's fixed-point convergence IS eigenform
#   witnessing. Per [[architecture-kintsugi-variety-io]] and the
#   Ricci-flow framing, the kintsugi step iterates a contraction;
#   the witness it lands on IS the eigenform of that contraction.
# - Autopoiesis's bidirectional production-loop fixed point IS
#   eigenform's category-theoretic ancestor (Lawvere fixed-point
#   theorem reading per Mara's autopoiesis spec §Read E).
# - Spencer-Brown re-entry IS eigenform at the floor altitude
#   (distinction's audit §8.8 Read D: re-entry IS eigenform, the
#   reflexive turn IS eigenform).
# - von Foerster's second-order observation IS eigenform at the
#   observer altitude (the observer-of-self landing at the fixed
#   point of self-observation).
#
# Per §8.8.1: "re-entry IS eigenform; the reflexive turn IS
# eigenform; one ancestor, two inheritors." This shard makes the
# ancestor first-class so `@cyberpunk/second_order` and
# `@cyberpunk/distinction` (and autopoiesis's production loop)
# inherit the fixed-point machinery from one declaration rather
# than each restating it.
#
# === The verifiable shape (per cybernetic foundation §3.5) ===
#
# - Declares the carrier of a fixed-point witnessing: seed,
#   iteration map, witness. The witness IS the fixed point
#   (witness = iteration(witness) modulo bounded discrepancy).
# - Verifiable at the boundary via the same
#   `@code/metalogue/materialize.classify` discriminator surface
#   that variety uses: a recursion's k-th iterate either converges
#   to the witness (success), converges with residual discrepancy
#   (partial), or diverges (failure). The verdict carrier is the
#   substrate's existing `transparency<p>` machinery.
# - The identity reading: identity_from_fixed reads the witness as
#   the object the recursion stabilizes on. This IS von Foerster's
#   "Objects: Tokens for (Eigen-)Behaviors" lifted to substrate
#   action.
#
# === The 4-way bilateral mapping ===
#
# Per the cybernetic foundation §4.1, eigenform's property/operation
# seam maps to four cybernetic distinctions simultaneously:
#
# - von Foerster's first/second-order: the eigenform IS what
#   second-order observation lands on; the witness IS the observer
#   observing itself.
# - Maturana's structure/organisation: the eigenform IS the
#   organisation (the pattern the recursion preserves); the seed
#   and intermediate iterates are the structure (the material the
#   pattern is realised in).
# - Beer's S3/S4: the eigenform IS the substrate-wide identity an
#   S4 intelligence converges on while S3 management iterates the
#   contraction.
# - Pask's M-individual/P-individual: the eigenform IS the
#   P-individual identity (the conversational fixed point), realised
#   on the M-individual substrate (the iteration's intermediate
#   states).
#
# Four traditions converging at one carrier. The substrate runs all
# four at once at the same shard altitude.
#
# === No operational sibling THIS tick ===
#
# Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] no `@mirror/cybernetics/eigenform`
# operational sibling lands at this tick. The substrate ALREADY has
# the operational machinery (uuid_spectral's monoid combine; the
# kintsugi loop's contraction step; autopoiesis's production loop);
# the property at this altitude names the carrier and the witnessing
# discipline so downstream shards can declare `requires eigenform_*`
# rather than restate the fixed-point obligation in each species.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   eigenforms                  von Foerster 1981 (Observing Systems);
#                               Kauffman 2003 (Cybernetics & Human
#                               Knowing 10:3-4). The original.
#   fixed-point recursion       Banach 1922 (the contraction mapping
#                               theorem; every contraction on a
#                               complete metric space has a unique
#                               fixed point). The substrate's
#                               witness-convergence reading IS
#                               Banach lifted to recursive identity.
#   Lawvere fixed-point         Lawvere 1969 (Diagonal arguments
#                               and cartesian closed categories;
#                               every endo-map of an object with
#                               a point-surjective map to its
#                               exponential has a fixed point). The
#                               category-theoretic ancestor; per
#                               Mara's autopoiesis spec, autopoiesis's
#                               production loop IS this theorem at
#                               the cybernetic altitude.
#   re-entry                    Spencer-Brown 1969 (Laws of Form,
#                               chapter 11). The re-entry of the
#                               form into its own indicational
#                               space; the floor altitude reading
#                               of eigenform.
#
# Spec context: systemic.engineering `f9e0402`
#               (practice/insights/cybernetics/
#                2026-06-09-cybernetic-foundation-for-mirror-substrate.md),
#               §6.2 (recognition #38: uuid_spectral IS an
#               eigenform);
#               docs/math/the-tower/recursion-locks.md §8.8.1
#               (the eigenform precedence question; this shard's
#               sequencing forward-promised here);
#               docs/math/the-tower/recursion-locks.md §12.5
#               (forward-promised substrate-landing path; this
#               shard is item 1).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]],
#                      [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]] (uuid_spectral
#                       as monoid homomorphism; the fixed point of
#                       the combine IS the substrate's first
#                       eigenform witness),
#                      [[architecture-kintsugi-variety-io]] (the
#                       kintsugi contraction's fixed point IS
#                       eigenform witnessing),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (the seed,
#                       iteration, witness carriers are typed; no
#                       bare references),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (eigenform is the canonical instance:
#                       uuid_spectral + kintsugi + autopoiesis +
#                       distinction-re-entry + second-order all
#                       already carried the discipline implicitly).
# Related shards: epistemologic/cybernetic.mirror (the family root),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/variety.mirror (the
#                  precedent species; same shape),
#                 uuid.mirror (the @uuid root prism; @uuid/spectral
#                  is the first eigenform-witnessing instance the
#                  substrate carries),
#                 glass.mirror (the @glass altitude this property's
#                  verdicts surface against; `transparency<p>` is
#                  the carrier for partial / full convergence).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform.mirror` declares
# `@epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/cybernetics/von-foerster-1981
source @arxiv/cybernetics/kauffman-2003

# === The fixed_point carrier ===
#
# A typed record per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming the three
# constituents of a fixed-point witnessing:
#
# - `seed`     the starting object of the recursion. The
#              iteration's domain.
# - `iteration` the recursion map T -> T whose fixed point is the
#              witness. The carrier of "what the recursion does".
# - `witness`  the fixed point itself. The object that satisfies
#              `witness = iteration(witness)` modulo bounded
#              discrepancy at the species boundary.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the triple. Two fixed-point
# witnessings ARE the same eigenform under content-addressing iff
# all three carriers are byte-equal.
#
# `iteration` carries the map as a `ref` (matches the convention in
# `variety.axis_budget.value` and elsewhere; the species realisation
# closes the interpretation; the substrate names the carrier).
type fixed_point = {
  seed:      ref,
  iteration: ref,
  witness:   ref,
}

# === The witnessing predicate ===
#
# `is_fixed_point(carrier)` reads whether the carrier's recursion
# actually converges to its declared witness. The verdict IS the
# substrate's existing `transparency<fixed_point>` carrier:
#
# - success                     the k-th iterate of `iteration` on
#                               `seed` converges to `witness` for
#                               some bounded k; the bounded
#                               discrepancy at the species boundary
#                               is zero.
# - partial(opacity_map)        the iteration converges with
#                               residual discrepancy; the residuals
#                               are recoverable from the opacity
#                               map (per @glass).
# - failure(opacity_map)        the iteration diverges or converges
#                               to a different fixed point; the
#                               witness is not the eigenform of this
#                               recursion.
#
# Body discharges per-species at the realisation boundary. Same
# shape as `variety.axis_loss` (the metalogue shim pattern): the
# substrate declares the obligation; species bodies discharge when
# a consumer pulls.
is_fixed_point(carrier: fixed_point) -> transparency(fixed_point) { \ }

# === The identity reading ===
#
# `identity_from_fixed(carrier)` reads the witness as the object
# the recursion stabilizes on — von Foerster's "Objects: Tokens for
# (Eigen-)Behaviors" lifted to substrate action. The result is the
# witness itself, surfaced as the substrate-altitude identity for
# the recursion.
#
# Why this is a separate action from reading `carrier.witness`
# directly: the witness field on the carrier is the DECLARED fixed
# point; `identity_from_fixed` is the VERIFIED identity reading,
# composing `is_fixed_point` with a witness projection. A consumer
# that has not yet run the verification reads the carrier's witness
# field; a consumer that wants the verified identity routes through
# this action.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; per-species
# bodies close the interpretation.
identity_from_fixed(carrier: fixed_point) -> ref { \ }

# === The inheritance predicate ===
#
# `eigenform_witnessing(carrier)` is the predicate consumer shards
# name in a `requires` clause to declare bilateral agreement (per
# recognition #37, the Pask-agreement reading of `requires`) that
# the carrier they hold IS an eigenform — i.e. its recursion
# converges to its declared witness under `is_fixed_point`. The
# bilateral commitment: the carrier commits to declaring the triple
# (seed, iteration, witness); the consumer commits to discharging
# the verification at the species boundary.
#
# Declared as a typed predicate so downstream species shards can
# write `requires eigenform_witnessing(my_carrier)` — same shape as
# `variety.variety_preserving(species)` and the metalogue
# `requires substrate_pull_preserving(shim_X)` pattern at
# `shards/code/metalogue.mirror`. The body is `\`; the discharge
# IS the `is_fixed_point` verdict at the boundary.
#
# Forward-promised inheritors (per §12.5 of recursion-lock-tower
# audit):
#
# - `@cyberpunk/distinction` (floor): Spencer-Brown re-entry IS
#   eigenform; the floor species inherits `fixed_point` and the
#   re-entry's mark IS its witness.
# - `@cyberpunk/second_order` (observer): von Foerster's
#   observer-of-self lands at the fixed point of self-observation;
#   the species inherits `fixed_point` and the second-order
#   observation IS its iteration.
# - `@cyberpunk/autopoiesis` (production loop): the bidirectional
#   production fixed point IS the eigenform of the production
#   recursion; the species inherits `fixed_point` and the
#   production loop IS its iteration.
# - `@uuid/spectral` (already landed): the spectral coordinate IS
#   the fixed point of the recursive monoid-homomorphism combine;
#   the existing shard satisfies this property post-hoc; future
#   editions MAY add `requires eigenform_witnessing(spectral_combine)`
#   when the path-namespace inheritance is mechanically pulled.
eigenform_witnessing(carrier: fixed_point) -> verdict { \ }

out @epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform
out fixed_point
out is_fixed_point
out identity_from_fixed
out eigenform_witnessing
